{{also|Sterben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|sterben}}, from {{inh|de|goh|sterban}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*sterbaną}}, itself either from {{der|de|ine-pro|*(s)terp-|t=to lose force; lose sensibility, become numb; be dead, be motionless}} or from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sterbʰ-|t=to be stiff, become stiff}}. Cognate with {{cog|nds|starven}}, {{m|nds|staarven}}, {{cog|nl|sterven}}, {{cog|fy|stjerre}}, {{cog|en|starve}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtɛʁbən/|[ˈʃtɛʁbən]|[ˈʃtɛɐ̯bən]|[ˈʃtɛʁbm̩]|[ˈʃtɛɐ̯bm̩]}}
* {{audio|de|De-sterben.ogg|Audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-sterben.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}
* {{rhyme|de|ɛʁbn̩|s=2}}
* {{hyph|de|ster|ben}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|sterben<stirbt#starb,gestorben,stürbe.sein>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[die]]
#: {{uxi|de|Mein Hund ist '''gestorben'''.|My dog has '''died'''.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with accusative or genitive}} to [[die]] of a (particular kind of) [[death]]
#: {{uxi|de|Das Opfer ist eines schrecklichen Todes '''gestorben'''.|The victim '''died''' a terrible death.}}

